-- check/good: two constraints on ONE variable, which is what pins §6.6's
-- rendering order and §6.5's layout. The clause is written `pick` before
-- `eq` and `render` before both; the scheme must print them sorted by
-- VARIABLE name as rendered, then by METHOD name text — so `a.eq` comes
-- before `a.pick`, and both before `b.render`. The interface record sorts
-- each variable's block the same way (§6.5 rule 1), and neither order is
-- the order they were written in.
pub choose : a, a, b → a
    where
        a.pick : a, a → a
        , b.render : b, Int → a
        , a.eq : a, a → Bool
choose x y tag = if x.eq y then tag.render 1 else x.pick y
